---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { privacy, providerPolicies, partner, links } from '../data/campaign';

/**
 * The privacy page. Deliberately NOT a legal template: it describes only what
 * this website actually does, names only the services that actually process
 * information through it, and claims nothing about the Privacy Act or the
 * Australian Privacy Principles, because the business structure and statutory
 * threshold have not been established.
 *
 * There is no reCAPTCHA section and no Google policy links, because reCAPTCHA
 * is disabled on the signup form. If it is ever turned back on, this page must
 * be updated before that change goes live.
 *
 * No Event structured data is emitted here. That lives in the Long Lunch
 * section, which only exists on the homepage.
 */
---
<Base
  title={privacy.title}
  description={privacy.description}
  socialTitle={privacy.title}
  socialDescription={privacy.description}
>
  <section class="section surface-light legal" aria-labelledby="privacy-title">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">The Long Road Home</p>
      <h1 id="privacy-title" class="display section-title">{privacy.heading}</h1>
      <hr class="rule" />
      <p class="updated">{privacy.updated}</p>

      <p class="lead">{privacy.intro}</p>

      <h2>Who runs this website</h2>
      <p>
        The Long Road Home website at thelongroadhome.com.au is owned and operated by
        {' '}{privacy.owner}, based in Brisbane, Australia. If you have a question about
        your information, email <a href={`mailto:${privacy.contactEmail}`}>{privacy.contactEmail}</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>What I collect</h2>
      <p>
        The signup form asks you to enter your name and email address. MailerLite and the
        website host may also process technical information as explained below.
      </p>
      <p>
        You only give me your name and email if you decide to subscribe. You can read the
        whole website without subscribing.
      </p>

      <h2>What I use it for</h2>
      <p>Your name and email address are used to send you:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>weekly updates on the journey</li>
        <li>announcements</li>
        <li>event invitations</li>
        <li>ways to get involved</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        I use your name and email address to send the communications listed above and to
        manage your subscription. Your name is there so the emails are not addressed to a
        stranger.
      </p>
      <p class="commitment">I do not sell or rent subscriber information.</p>

      <h2>MailerLite manages the list</h2>
      <p>
        My subscriber list is managed by MailerLite, and MailerLite sends the emails. When
        you subscribe, your name and email address are stored on their service.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you subscribe, MailerLite will send you a confirmation email. Your subscription
        starts only after you confirm it.
      </p>
      <p>
        MailerLite may also collect technical information and use cookies, tracking
        technologies and email performance data, such as whether an email was delivered,
        opened, or had a link clicked. What they collect and why is set out in the
        {' '}<a href={providerPolicies.mailerlite} rel="noopener">MailerLite privacy policy</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>How long I keep your information</h2>
      <p class="commitment">
        I keep subscriber information while someone remains subscribed. After they
        unsubscribe, MailerLite may retain the minimum record needed to make sure they are
        not emailed again.
      </p>

      <h2>Vercel hosts the website</h2>
      <p>
        The website is hosted by Vercel. As with any web host, Vercel processes the normal
        technical information needed to deliver the pages to your browser and keep the site
        secure and available. See the
        {' '}<a href={providerPolicies.vercel} rel="noopener">Vercel privacy notice</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Tickets are handled by TryBooking</h2>
      <p>
        Tickets to the Long Lunch are sold through TryBooking. When you book, you leave this
        website and complete the purchase on TryBooking's own site. Payment details are
        entered and processed through TryBooking, not through this website.
      </p>
      <p>
        What TryBooking collects when you book, and how it handles that information, is set
        out in the
        {' '}<a href={providerPolicies.trybooking} rel="noopener">TryBooking privacy policy</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Donations are handled by Top Blokes Foundation</h2>
      <p>
        The homepage can show a donation form provided by Raisely for Top Blokes Foundation.
        It is not loaded when you open the page. Nothing is requested from Raisely until you
        choose to load the form, by pressing the Donate button or the load button in the
        donation section. Until then, no part of it runs on the page.
      </p>
      <p>
        Once it loads, the form appears inside this website, but it is Raisely's form and it
        comes from Raisely. Anything you enter into it, including your details and payment
        information, is sent to Raisely and the payment services it uses, not to this
        website.
      </p>
      <p>
        Top Blokes Foundation controls the Raisely campaign and receives the donor
        information. Lachlan Stuart and The Long Road Home do not receive or store donor
        information or payment details, whether you use the form on this website or on
        Raisely.
      </p>
      <p>
        Loading the form may cause Raisely, and the payment, security, spam protection and
        analytics services its form uses, to process the ordinary technical information
        needed to show it to you, such as your IP address and browser details, and to use
        cookies or store information in your browser. That processing is carried out by
        those services, not by this website.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you would rather not load the form here at all, you can
        {' '}<a href={links.fundraising} rel="noopener">open the campaign page on Raisely</a>,
        which Top Blokes Foundation controls, and donate there instead.
      </p>
      <p>
        Read the
        {' '}<a href={providerPolicies.topBlokes} rel="noopener">Top Blokes Foundation Privacy Policy</a>
        {' '}and <a href={providerPolicies.raisely} rel="noopener">Raisely Privacy Policy</a> for
        details about how they handle information.
      </p>

      <h2>Partnership enquiries</h2>
      <p>
        The partnership button opens your own email application with a message addressed to
        {' '}{partner.name} at {partner.organisation}. There is no enquiry form on this
        website and no enquiry database behind it. Whatever you write goes from your email
        account to his, the same as any other email you send.
      </p>

      <h2>Websites I link to</h2>
      <p>
        This website also links out to Top Blokes Foundation, States of Mind, Instagram, Strava and
        my own website at lachlanstuart.com.au. This website does not embed content from
        those services. If you follow one of the links, you leave The Long Road Home website
        and the other service's privacy practices apply.
      </p>

      <h2>Your information may be processed outside Australia</h2>
      <p>
        MailerLite and Vercel provide services to this website, and in doing so they may
        store or process information outside Australia. I am not able to tell you which
        country that will be in your case, because it depends on how each provider runs its
        own infrastructure and that can change. Rather than guess, I would point you at
        their current privacy policies, linked above, which are the accurate source on where
        and how they handle information.
      </p>
      <p>
        TryBooking is different again. You reach it by choosing to follow a link and leaving
        this website, and from that point it handles your information as its own service,
        under its own privacy policy.
      </p>
      <p>
        Raisely provides the donation form on this website, and it and the services its
        form uses handle what they collect under their own privacy policies, linked above.
        Those policies are the accurate source on where that information is stored or
        processed.
      </p>

      <h2>Unsubscribing</h2>
      <p>
        Every email I send has an unsubscribe link at the bottom. Use it and you come off
        the list. You do not have to give a reason and you do not have to ask me first.
      </p>

      <h2>Asking about, correcting or deleting your information</h2>
      <p>
        Email <a href={`mailto:${privacy.contactEmail}`}>{privacy.contactEmail}</a> if you
        want to know what information I hold about you, or you want it corrected or deleted.
        Tell me the email address you subscribed with so I can find you.
      </p>

      <h2>Analytics and advertising</h2>
      <p>
        As at the date at the top of this page, this website has no first party analytics,
        no advertising pixels and no behavioural advertising. I am telling you what is true
        now rather than making a promise about the future. If that changes in a way that
        matters, I will update this page.
      </p>
      <p>
        The Raisely donation form on the homepage is separate. It is provided by Raisely, it
        loads only if you choose to load it, and as explained above, Raisely and the services
        its form uses, including analytics services, may collect technical information and
        set cookies at that point. This website does not receive that information.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to this page</h2>
      <p>
        If the way this website handles information materially changes, I will update this
        page and change the date at the top.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .legal { padding-block: var(--space-9) var(--space-9); }
  .updated {
    font-family: var(--font-support); font-weight: 600; font-size: var(--size-label);
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-label); text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--terrain); margin: var(--space-5) 0 0;
  }
  .legal h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-support); font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.125rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.02em; color: var(--on-light-1);
    margin: var(--space-7) 0 var(--space-3);
  }
  .legal ul { margin: 0 0 var(--space-4); padding-left: var(--space-5); max-width: var(--measure); }
  .legal li { margin-bottom: var(--space-2); line-height: var(--leading-body); color: var(--on-light-2); }
  .legal a { color: var(--terrain); text-underline-offset: 0.18em; }
  .legal a:hover, .legal a:focus-visible { color: var(--near); }
  /* The two operating commitments read slightly stronger than the surrounding
     explanation, because they are undertakings rather than description. */
  .commitment { color: var(--on-light-1); font-weight: 600; }
</style>
